Source: https://code.qt.io/playground/qlitehtml.git (src/ only; litehtml comes from the system package)

Local patches:
- container_qpainter.cpp draw_text(): draw at the font baseline instead of into a
  top-aligned clipping rect, so words containing fallback-font glyphs keep their
  baseline and descenders aren't clipped.
- container_qpainter.cpp text_width(): use QFontMetricsF (fractional widths)
  instead of integer QFontMetrics, so word spacing doesn't drift.
- qlitehtmlwidget.cpp render(): skip the litehtml relayout when the layout
  width hasn't changed (showing the window or a height-only resize).
- container_qpainter.cpp/_p.h: decode images lazily on first draw; layout uses
  the size from the image header (QImageReader::size()).
